message: "If you cite this computational research thesis, please use the metadata below. No DOI is minted here; do not invent one."
type: thesis
title: "Hybrid occult mode switches under sparse delayed liquid-biopsy-style partial observers"
authors:
  - family-names: Ogbonna
    given-names: Kelechi Emeka
    email: kelechiogbonna300@gmail.com
    alias: cloudynirvana
abstract: >-
  Which hybrid occult mode switches remain practically identifiable when the
  observation map is a sparse, delayed liquid-biopsy-style partial observer
  rather than a full state schedule? On a three-coordinate toy that inherits
  the mode names of Thesis #4, a full state schedule separates proliferative
  continuation, quiescence, angiogenic pause, and immune-held latency. A dense
  burden channel still separates them when the two pauses have different
  burden balances. The sparse delayed scalar keeps those separations while a
  burden gap remains, and it loses the angiogenic-versus-immune contrast when
  the two pauses are given the same burden law. That contrast is then carried
  only by the cycling and vascular coordinates, which the scalar does not see.
  Switch time in an arm that never leaves the proliferative field has Fisher
  information zero on every map. The scalar is not a ctDNA assay. Not a
  medical device. No cure.
keywords:
